  "body": "Add tone mapping to canvas\n\nAdd the `CanvasToneMapping` dictionary and `CanvasToneMappingMode` enum (`\"standard\"` and `\"extended\"`), and a `toneMapping` member to `CanvasRenderingContext2DSettings`, reflected by `getContextAttributes()`. These replace WebGPU's `GPUCanvasToneMapping` and `GPUCanvasToneMappingMode`, which WebGPU will reference from HTML in the same way it references `PredefinedColorSpace`.\n\nWhen a canvas is rendered to the output device, it is now tone mapped to the device's HDR headroom, as limited by `dynamic-range-limit`, before color space conversion.\n\nThis has been the planned trajectory of the API since [its proposal to WebGPU](https://github.com/ccameron-chromium/webgpu-hdr/blob/main/EXPLAINER.md#notes-on-canvasrenderingcontext2d-and-unification-of-apis). Its move from WebGPU-only to HTML was waiting for float16 support for 2D canvas and WebGL.\n\nFixes https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11424\n\n- [X] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium: Proposed\n   * Gecko: [No feedback](https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/1359)\n   * WebKit: [Supportive](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11734#issuecomment-6140323936)\n- [X] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/62367\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: [https://crbug.com/448552449](https://crbug.com/448552449)\n   * Gecko: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2091636\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=330852\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\n    * https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46476\n- [X] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message]\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11734/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 6:43 AM UTC (42269c8)\">/canvas.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11734/24c5e48...42269c8/canvas.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 6:43 AM UTC (42269c8)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11734/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 6:43 AM UTC (42269c8)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11734/24c5e48...42269c8/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 6:43 AM UTC (42269c8)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11734/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 6:43 AM UTC (42269c8)\">/references.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11734/24c5e48...42269c8/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 6:43 AM UTC (42269c8)\">diff</a> )",
